Explanation:

1. User requests website by opening a web browser and enetering www.foobar.com

2. The domain name is foobar.com, its purpose is to provide a human-readable name for the website instead of making users rememeber IP addresses of the server

3. wwww is configured as an A record pointing to 8.8.8.8, which maps a hostname to an IPv4 address

4. The server at 8.8.8.8 is a computer that provides services and resources to other computers over a network. This server contains nginx, app server, app files, MySQL

5. Nginx/web server receives the HTTP requests from clients and can return static files such as HTML/CSS, otherwise this will pass the request to the app server if it requires application logic.

6. The app server is responsible for running the application's backend code, runs when dynamic processing is required from the web server.

7. Application files are the actual code of the website, which can include python files, api endpoints, flask routes, etc.

8. MySQL Database stores the application's persistent data. The application communicates with MySQL when it needs to retrieve, create, modify or delete stored info. (CRUM)

9. The server communicates with the user's computer by using HTTP over TCP/IP.

Issues with the Infrastructure:

1. SPOF, aka single point of failure refers to when everything is located on one server, which the main probl;em is if that one server goes down, there is no backup server to take over and clients are not able to access any servers.

2. Maintenance causes downtime, since there is only one server, there is no other server that can process requests in the downtime while the maintenance is happening.

3. One server cannot handle unlimited traffic as the server will have limited CPU power, RAM, disk resources, etc.